# Ask module public boundary

## Scope

Applies to `ui/src/components/work/ask/**` and external consumers of Ask (`ui/src/pages/**`, `ui/src/components/work/traceability/**`, etc.).

## Rule

- Treat `ui/src/components/work/ask/index.js` as the **only public entrypoint** for Ask exports.
- From outside `ask/`, do not import from `ask/shell/*`, `ask/session/*`, `ask/chat/*`, `ask/answer/*`, `ask/forms/*`, or `ask/orchestration/*`.
- If an external module needs a new Ask symbol, re-export it from `ask/index.js` first, then import from `ask/index.js`.

## Internal structure intent

- `shell/` -> `orchestration/` -> (`session/`, `chat/`, `answer/`, `forms/`)
- Avoid reverse dependencies from leaf domains back into `shell/` or page-level modules.

## Agent integration (Ask → agent)

- Ask UI may depend on agent presentation components; import them from **`ui/src/components/work/agent/index.js`** (narrow export surface) instead of deep paths under `agent/*` implementation files.
- When adding a new cross-import from `ask/` to `agent/`, extend `agent/index.js` first.

## Verification checklist (after Ask refactors)

- `rg "components/work/ask/" ui/src` should show external imports using `ask/index.js` only.
- `npm run lint`
- `npm run test -- src/components/work/ask src/components/work/traceability/askFlowCompatibility.test.js`
